The CPU sensor uses first-return Amanatides-Woo traversal of the declared
0.1 m voxelized scene at finite body-frame FoV angular sampling. Only the
renderer sees scene truth. XYZI rays are world-frame acquisition-stamped:
intensity=1 means a first hit; 0 means a measured clear ray to max range.
Missing frames are not misses. GridMap matches the acquisition odometry,
fuses free traversed cells and occupied endpoints, and retains observed map
memory. It does not grant free status to the whole FoV or behind hits.
This is a geometric simulation sensor, not an optical/acoustic device model.
The existing Swarm global guide and local trajectory optimization are retained.
The observed-map mode can subscribe to the same analytic survey rays consumed
by task execution, avoiding a second obstacle sampling model. In that explicit
mode unknown and out-of-map positions are blocked through the existing shared
collision accessor. Legacy launches retain their prior occupancy semantics.
This sampled planning guard is not a continuous-time tracking safety proof.

Explicit known-free deployment boxes seed navigation only. Declared forbidden
boxes remain navigation policy, not sensor hits or occluders. A valid scan also
updates the sensor-origin voxel skipped by the upstream reverse ray traversal.

